{
  "architecture": "Three repos, one contract. `POST /tournaments/:id/register` (tournaments.controller.ts:1135-1151) → `TournamentRegistrationService.register` (tournament-registration.service.ts) → `TournamentsRepository.registerParticipant` (tournament-registration.repository.ts, delegating through tournaments.repository.ts:795-799). Division resolution is implemented twice on purpose: a service-level pre-flight (validates ELO + gender, never mutates the DTO) and an in-transaction, tournament-scoped re-resolution that is the authoritative guard and the only place that persists `tournamentDivisionId` (repository:1038). Clients are three: `web` (quick-create + register flows, `quickTournamentFormats.ts`), `app` Flutter (`quick_tournament_format_mapping.dart`…
  "files": [
    {
      "description": "Register DTO. `divisionId` (44-47) and `tournamentDivisionId` (49-52) are BOTH `@IsOptional() @IsUUID('4')` — the contract genuinely has no required division field, which is why the missing-id path must stay well-defined.",
      "path": "backend/src/modules/tournaments/dto/register-tournament.dto.ts"
    },
    {
      "description": "Service-level division resolution (334-350), gender requirement (351-357), match-type fallback (359-360), ELO+gender validation against the RESOLVED division (459-463), and the unchanged DTO hand-off to the repository (465-470).",
      "path": "backend/src/modules/tournaments/services/tournament-registration.service.ts"
    },
    {
      "description": "Authoritative in-transaction resolution: divisions query excludes CANCELLED (219-228), `requestedDivisionId = data.tournamentDivisionId ?? data.divisionId` (230-231), >1 active with no id → 400 (232-235), single-active fallback (237-241), `isExplicitOpenDivision` (285-302), `selectedDivision = requestedDivision` + hard 400 when unresolvable (374-394), participant insert persisting `tournamentDivisionId: selectedDivision?.id ?? null` (1038).",
      "path": "backend/src/modules/tournaments/repositories/tournament-registration.repository.ts"
    },
    {
      "description": "`joinLite` 0/1/many rules (1176-1190) and the conditional spread that omits `tournamentDivisionId` (1257-1259); `addLiteClubMember` legacy caller that omits it too (1428-1439).",
      "path": "backend/src/modules/tournaments/services/tournament-lite.service.ts"
    },
    {
      "description": "Endpoints: `POST :id/register` (1135-1151) accepts the DTO verbatim; `POST join/:inviteCode` (152-165) routes into the same `register`; `POST lite/join/:inviteCode` (754-766) takes `@Body('divisionId') divisionId: string | undefined`.",
      "path": "backend/src/modules/tournaments/tournaments.controller.ts"
    },
    {
      "description": "`isGenderUnrestricted` (63-73) — the predicate that makes an open division (null/unrestricted token) skip the profile-gender requirement.",
      "path": "backend/src/common/helpers/gender.helper.ts"
    },
    {
      "description": "Executable statement of the intended contract: ID-less registration uses the sole active division; ID-less is rejected when multiple active divisions exist; open formats need no profile gender; restricted divisions still do; phone stays required.",
      "path": "backend/src/modules/tournaments/services/tournament-registration-open-format.spec.ts"
    },
    {
      "description": "`OPEN_SINGLES`/`OPEN_DOUBLES` declared at 10-11; kept off the default cards by 22-25; `genderRestrictionByFormat` (39-46) has NO open entry; `toDivisionInput` maps `includes('SINGLES')` → SINGLES else DOUBLES (60-64) and omits the key via `...(genderRestriction ? {genderRestriction} : {})` (65).",
      "path": "web/src/app/organizer/tournaments/create/quickTournamentFormats.ts"
